content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-105, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22000, filtered-water line (sodium hypochlorite dosed)",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.9 mm/s is in Zone B (2.8 to 4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation') of the HF-300 severity chart. It is below Zone C (4.5) and well below Zone D (7.1, 'stop the pump'). The SSP-07 immediate-stop rule applies only in the manufacturer's highest zone (Zone D), so it does not apply. The report does not say whether this is the highest RMS reading from both bearing housings, which is how the manual says to classify vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature 71 C is 1 C above the manufacturer's normal limit (up to 70 C). It is below the alarm limit (80 C) and the trip limit (90 C). The SSP-07 priority-1 rule applies only above the alarm limit, so it is not triggered. The reading is still elevated and needs investigation.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage at the shaft seal is a confirmed defect. The manual's corrective action is to replace the mechanical seal (5.2) and check alignment (5.4). The seal must never run dry (Plan 11 flush from discharge). The leaking fluid is sodium hypochlorite-dosed water.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Priority set to P2. No P1 or immediate-stop trigger is met (vibration Zone B; temperature below the 80 C alarm). The active chemical seal leak and above-normal bearing temperature justify planned repair rather than routine scheduling.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked seal faces. This may be the documented early failure of component seal HF3-450 on pumps from serial HF3-22000, caused by a revised sleeve tolerance. This applies if an HF3-450 is currently fitted.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. This is listed as a cause of all three reported symptoms: seal leakage, raised vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal run dry, for example through loss of the Plan 11 flush.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear or over-greasing, which would explain the 71 C housing temperature and contribute to vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Obtain permits and apply controls. Electrically isolate and LOTO at the MCC. Close and lock the suction and discharge valves. Raise a line-break permit and drain and vent the pump before opening it. Prepare a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before shutdown, record vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading against Figure 3. Also record the drive-end temperature, to give an as-found baseline.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller. Withdraw the seal and shaft sleeve. Record which seal part number was fitted (HF3-450 or HF3-450B).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 for scoring. Replace it if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. No sleeve setting measurement is needed for the pre-set HF3-450B.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the drive-end and non-drive-end bearings and check grease quantity. If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both as a pair (5.3).",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit cartridge seal HF3-450B. Do NOT fit HF3-450. Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten fasteners on lightly oiled threads: seal gland nuts (M10) 30 Nm per SB-2026-014; impeller nut (M24) 160 Nm; casing bolts (M16) 210 Nm; bearing housing bolts (M12) 85 Nm if disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align the shaft (required after work that moves the motor or bearing housing, and recommended for seal leakage). Tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm; angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm the Plan 11 seal flush is open and the pump is primed so the seal never runs dry. Remove isolations under the permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, re-measure vibration on both housings and the drive-end temperature. Confirm vibration is in Zone A/B, temperature is at or below 70 C, and there is no seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set (supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve (conditional: fit only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (conditional: replace as a pair with HF3-510 if worn)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (conditional: replace as a pair with HF3-512 if worn)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC. Mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves. Line-break permit, with the pump drained and vented first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, above the 25 kg threshold. A lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-105 is on a sodium hypochlorite-dosed line and the seal is leaking. Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C16",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the seal dry. Confirm the Plan 11 flush before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration enters Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s) at any time, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingent bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h, 2 technicians, only if bearings are found worn.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part: the manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450, but SB-2026-014 (issued 14 Mar 2026) supersedes it with cartridge seal HF3-450B for serial HF3-22000 and above. P-105 is serial HF3-22000, which is inside the 'and above' range. Therefore HF3-450B applies and HF3-450 must not be fitted.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm, while SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. The bulletin applies to this serial, so use 30 Nm. Only pumps below HF3-22000 keep Table 5 / 25 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve check: manual 5.2 calls for sleeve inspection, while the bulletin says HF3-450B is pre-set with no sleeve measurement needed. It also adds a replacement criterion of scoring deeper than 0.1 mm. Apply the bulletin: no setting measurement, but still inspect the sleeve for scoring against the 0.1 mm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which seal part number is currently fitted to P-105 (HF3-450 or HF3-450B)? This affects the root-cause conclusion.",
    "Is 3.9 mm/s the highest RMS reading across both bearing housings, as Figure 3 classification requires? Where was it measured?",
    "Torques for other fasteners (impeller nut, casing bolts, bearing housing bolts) are not restated in the bulletin. The bulletin says only pumps below HF3-22000 'continue to use Table 5'. Confirm with AquaDyne that Table 5 values other than gland torque still apply to serial HF3-22000 and above.",
    "Grease type, quantity and relubrication interval for the bearings are not given in the evidence, so over-greasing cannot be checked against a specification.",
    "The manual does not define what temperature counts as 'high temperature' for bearing replacement (5.3). It is unclear whether 71 C (above normal, below alarm) alone justifies bearing replacement.",
    "Labour time in Table 6 may reflect the original component seal. The time for pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B is not documented.",
    "Leak rate and severity, and whether hypochlorite exposure makes immediate shutdown advisable, are not stated in the report.",
    "Status of the Plan 11 seal flush (whether the seal may have run dry) is not reported."
  ]
}
